  "turns": [
    {
      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Required solver: OpenSees.\nAnalyze the attached 6 m single-bay steel frame in OpenSees using the stated absolute elevations. Both column bases are fixed at z=-1.5 m. An unloaded, full-span, rigidly connected ground tie beam joins the column lines at z=0; two upper floor beams are at z=2.1 m and z=5.7 m. Only these upper beams carry 10 kN/m downward in case D. Report ux/uz/ry at all ground and upper beam-column joints, separate upper-minus-lower Δux/Δuz for every actual column segment, N/V3/M2 at both tie-beam ends, and Fx/Fz/My at both bases. Use the explicit appendix properties and axes for first-order linear elastic static analysis with self-weight disabled.\n\nUse all public appendices. Report the complete requested numerical table and the required summaries.",
      "state": 1,
      "expectation": "analyze",
      "attachments": [
        "input-data.json",
        "output-requests.json",
        "analysis-conventions.txt",
